Practice out loud. Walk in ready.
What is MockMic?
MockMic is a voice-first mock interview practice app. Users answer AI-generated interview questions out loud (or by typing as a fallback), get instant structured feedback, and build confidence through tracked, repeated practice sessions.
Day 3 Objective
Build the project's foundation before any feature development begins — a fully working, empty shell that Day 4 can build directly on top of.
What Was Completed Today
Development environment configured — Node.js, Git, VS Code, Vercel CLI, and Firebase CLI installed and verified
Project folder structure created — matches the architecture locked on Day 2 (public/ for frontend, api/ for Vercel serverless functions)
Git repository initialized — connected to GitHub with a defined branching strategy (main for stable code, dev for active work)
Firebase project connected — Authentication and Firestore reachable from the app
Configuration files completed — .env.local, .gitignore, package.json, vercel.json
"Hello World" version running locally — confirms the full chain (frontend → Vercel function → Firebase) is wired correctly
